    {
      "url": "https://github.com/TombStoneDash/lims-box/issues/94",
      "title": "Restore automatic Personnel Pack PDF fulfillment",
      "issue_number": 94,
      "body": "## Incident\n\nA production Personnel Pack request on 2026-08-26 was captured, but the internal fallback notice reported that no PDF URL is configured and manual fulfillment is required.\n\nNo applicant name, email address, organization, or request-specific PII is included here.\n\n## Impact\n\n- lead capture succeeds;\n- the applicant does not receive the requested Personnel Pack automatically;\n- support must acknowledge and fulfill each request manually;\n- a configured accreditation selection cannot produce a verified download.\n\n## Containment completed\n\nThe affected applicant received one manual acknowledgment from Tombstone Dash Gmail. Do not send a duplicate acknowledgment.\n\n## Required repair\n\n1. Identify the intended source-of-truth Personnel Pack PDF for each supported accreditation type.\n2. Verify each asset contains only approved public/demo content and no customer data.\n3. Configure the production download URL through the existing secret/configuration path.\n4. Make the applicant confirmation include a working, access-controlled or public download as intended.\n5. Add regression coverage for configured and missing-PDF behavior.\n6. Run one production-safe external-inbox test proving the confirmation and download both work.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- supported accreditation selections map to approved assets;\n- no fallback/manual-fulfillment notice on the test;\n- external confirmation arrives once;\n- download returns the intended PDF;\n- no applicant PII appears in issues, fixtures, logs, or receipts;\n- production proof is timestamped before closure.",
