    {
      "url": "https://github.com/TombStoneDash/lims-box/issues/95",
      "title": "Audit inactive Google OAuth clients before deletion",
      "issue_number": 95,
      "body": "## Alert\n\nGoogle Developers reported on 2026-08-27 that the `lims-box` Google Cloud project has OAuth clients inactive for at least five months and scheduled for automatic deletion in 30 days.\n\nNo client IDs, secrets, account data, or customer information are included here.\n\n## Required work\n\n1. Inventory the inactive OAuth clients in the `lims-box` Google Cloud project.\n2. Map each client to its current production, preview, local, or retired use without exposing credentials.\n3. For every client still required, exercise it through a legitimate Sign in with Google flow or refresh-token exchange before the deadline.\n4. Allow truly retired clients to expire or remove them deliberately.\n5. Verify current LIMS BOX authentication in production and the supported development environment after the audit.\n6. Record privacy-safe proof and the final keep/retire disposition for each client.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Every listed inactive client has one owner and a keep/retire decision.\n- Required clients are exercised before 2026-09-26 and remain valid.\n- Retired clients are not referenced by deployed configuration.\n- Production authentication is verified without logging tokens, client secrets, or user PII.",
